$ HA144A full-span — Step 63 free-flight maneuver x MASSSET payload sweep
$
$ Purpose: the full "maneuvers x payload conditions" demonstration (G0-b).
$ One deck, one elevator ramp-and-hold command shape, three payload conditions
$ — each subcase runs the FREE-FLIGHT modal transient solver (MLOADS
$ METHOD=-1): the rigid states (ANGLEA/PITCH/URDD3/URDD5) are integrated, not
$ prescribed, so the maneuver self-balances (closure ~ 0) and each mass case
$ settles at its own load factor.  The fuel tanks sit at the baseline CG
$ (fwd/aft fuselage split), so the sweep is a near-pure mass change and the
$ physics check holds: heavier case => lower steady NZ_REL for the same
$ elevator increment.
$
$   MASSSET 10  EMPTY     16000 lb   baggage DELETEd
$   MASSSET 20  HALFFUEL  18500 lb   + 2500 lb fuselage fuel (ADD)
$   MASSSET 30  FULLFUEL  21000 lb   + 5000 lb fuel + baggage 500->1000 (REPLACE)
$
$ MLDCOMD tables are ABSOLUTE and therefore mass-case-specific: each subcase
$ has its own MLOADS/MLDCOMD/TABLED1 whose t=0 value is that case's trim ELEV
$ (two-pass authoring — trim first, then author the table from the trim value).
$
$ Bulk model: ha144a_fullspan_sbeam.bdf + Step 60 mass cases; TRIM 1 carries
$ RHOREF (mandatory for free flight: V = sqrt(2q/rho) feeds B_hh).
$
$ Outputs per subcase: .f06 maneuver block (MODAL SOLVER + FREE FLIGHT lines),
$ .mldprnt.txt time history (with NZ_REL), .maneuver_qs_loads.bdf critical loads.
$
$ Units: ft, lb, slug, s
$
SOL 144
TITLE = HA144A free-flight MLOADS x MASSSET sweep
$ Subcase 1 — EMPTY (MASSSET 10)
SUBCASE 1
  MLOADS  = 10
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 10
$ Subcase 2 — HALF FUEL (MASSSET 20)
SUBCASE 2
  MLOADS  = 20
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 20
$ Subcase 3 — FULL FUEL (MASSSET 30)
SUBCASE 3
  MLOADS  = 30
  SPC     = 1
  MASSSET = 30
BEGIN BULK
$
