CONM2, 5000, 98, 0, 15.5405
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------
$ OVERLAY CONM2s — referenced by a MASSSET ADD / REPLACE-overlay slot,
$ so they are excluded from the baseline mass and only enter the cases
$ that name them.  The fwd (GRID 98, x=10) / aft (GRID 99, x=20) tank
$ split is 30/70 so the fuel CG sits at the baseline CG (x ~ 17) — the
$ payload sweep is a near-pure mass change (no D4 mean-axis warning).
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Half fuel: 600 lb fwd + 1900 lb aft = 2500 lb
CONM2, 6001, 98, 0, 18.6486
CONM2, 6002, 99, 0, 43.5134
$ Full fuel: 1200 lb fwd + 3800 lb aft = 5000 lb
CONM2, 6011, 98, 0, 37.2972
CONM2, 6012, 99, 0, 87.0268
$ Heavy baggage (1000 lb) — replaces baseline CONM2 5000 in the FULL case
CONM2, 6020, 98, 0, 31.0810
$
$ ============================================================
$ MASS CASES (Step 60) — selected per subcase by case-control MASSSET
$ ============================================================
MASSSET, 10, EMPTY, 1.0
+, DELETE, 5000
MASSSET, 20, HALFFUEL, 1.0
+, ADD, 6001, 6002
MASSSET, 30, FULLFUEL, 1.0
+, ADD, 6011, 6012
+, REPLACE, 5000, 6020
$
$ ============================================================
$ CONSTRAINTS — FULL-SPAN single-point ground (NOT the half-model symmetry BC).
$   A full-span model must NOT carry the half-model's centreline symmetry SPCs
$   (Ty,Rx,Rz along 97-100): those ground fuselage torsion and give the wing
$   roots a rigid wall instead of the real wing->fuselage->wing load path, and
$   they bake the symmetry assumption into what is meant to be an independent
$   check.  Instead pin the 4 non-trim rigid-body modes (Tx,Ty,Rx,Rz) at the
$   single reference point GRID 90; SUPORT carries the 2 symmetric trim DOF
$   (Tz,Ry).  Under symmetric loads the antisymmetric DOF come out ~0 with no
$   SPC needed, so the structure deforms freely (both wings react through the
$   fuselage, not against a rigid centreline).
$ ============================================================
SPC1, 1, 1246, 90
SUPORT, 90, 35
$
$ ============================================================
$ AERODYNAMIC PANELS  (CAERO1 EIDs sorted: 1000,1100,2000,2100)
$ ============================================================
PAERO1, 1000
